00:54:25.036 --> 00:54:27.740
Do me a favor and stay here.


00:54:29.644 --> 00:54:31.047
Are you sure?


00:54:33.018 --> 00:54:34.654
Yeah.


00:54:35.724 --> 00:54:38.126
Scream if something goes wrong.


00:54:38.128 --> 00:54:39.164
I'm here.


00:55:19.711 --> 00:55:22.014
Lisa Grigorieva.


00:55:22.016 --> 00:55:23.685
Take what's yours.


00:55:24.454 --> 00:55:26.122
Give me the loved one.


00:55:42.757 --> 00:55:45.295
<i>When I was a kid,
I had a dream.</i>


00:55:49.037 --> 00:55:51.172
I'm in the house, alone.


00:55:51.174 --> 00:55:54.513
Parents are out.


00:55:54.515 --> 00:55:58.255
And then suddenly, I
hear someone outside.


00:56:00.927 --> 00:56:04.868
<i>He says, "Open the door,"
but I don't open it.</i>


00:56:08.943 --> 00:56:12.450
<i>And the door slowly
opens, all by itself.</i>


00:56:16.057 --> 00:56:17.993
<i>Hinges creak.</i>


00:56:17.995 --> 00:56:20.032
The deadbolt turns.


00:56:22.136 --> 00:56:26.111
Somehow, I'm on my
way to open the door.


00:56:28.916 --> 00:56:31.122
Mom is standing there.


00:56:34.193 --> 00:56:37.064
She looks at me and whispers,


00:56:37.066 --> 00:56:42.442
"I'm taking the one who's
home alone, the one you love"


00:56:42.444 --> 00:56:44.013
<i>And I'm scared.</i>


00:57:10.633 --> 00:57:13.238
Do you love me?


00:57:19.585 --> 00:57:21.152
I do.


00:57:27.534 --> 00:57:30.070
Did you hear that?


00:57:30.072 --> 00:57:31.275
Roma?


00:57:32.577 --> 00:57:34.046
Roma.


00:57:35.483 --> 00:57:37.384
What are you doing?


00:57:37.386 --> 00:57:38.587
Take me.


00:57:38.589 --> 00:57:40.023
Roma.


00:57:40.025 --> 00:57:41.527
I can't
bear this anymore.


00:57:41.529 --> 00:57:43.130
Take me.


00:57:43.132 --> 00:57:44.435
Roma!


00:57:45.503 --> 00:57:46.603
What are you doing?


00:57:46.605 --> 00:57:48.173
- Enough.
- I can't bear it.


00:57:48.175 --> 00:57:51.145
- That's enough!
- I can't do this anymore.


00:58:11.120 --> 00:58:13.289
Lisa Grigorieva,
take what's yours


00:58:13.291 --> 00:58:15.463
and give me the loved one.


00:58:28.154 --> 00:58:30.658
<i>We used to tell
fortunes with my mom for fun.</i>


00:58:30.660 --> 00:58:32.862
<i>We'd look into two mirrors
opposite each other</i>


00:58:32.864 --> 00:58:36.137
<i>and see if we can
spot Mr. Right.</i>


00:59:02.289 --> 00:59:05.829
Lisa Grigorieva,
take what's yours


00:59:05.831 --> 00:59:07.432
and give me the loved one.


00:59:39.832 --> 00:59:41.767
Do you love me?


00:59:41.769 --> 00:59:43.606
More than life itself.


00:59:59.772 --> 01:00:00.808
Look who's here.


01:00:03.680 --> 01:00:04.749
No, no, go.


01:00:06.752 --> 01:00:09.422
You said you loved
me more than life itself.


01:00:15.536 --> 01:00:17.572
Go away.


01:00:17.574 --> 01:00:19.509
<i>He doesn't love you.</i>


01:00:19.511 --> 01:00:22.650
<i>Go away, go away,
go away, go away!</i>


